<title>UK: EIB sets 10 billion escudo five-year bond. [CORRECTED 11:36 GMT]</title>
<headline>EIB sets 10 billion escudo five-year bond. [CORRECTED 11:36 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers BPI, Caixa and Generale.</p>
<p> BORROWER   EUROPEAN INVESTMENT BANK</p>
<p> AMT    10 BLN PTE    COUPON    *5.75	MATURITY    24.JUN.02</p>
<p>					   (Corrects MATURITY date from May)</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE    24.JUN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  25 BP     LISTING    LUX	 SPREAD	5 BP</p>
<p> NOTES     *OPTION TO CONVERT THE ISSUE INTO FRN PAYING 6M LIBOR</p>
<p>		+ 5 BP ON ANY COUPON DATE.</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AAA/AAA   DENOMS (K) =	   SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF AN MTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
